// mecatl public API surface (WP10).
//
// HarnessService is the network surface over the WP8 agent loop. The
// primary RPC is the bidi `Converse` stream: the client sends a mandatory
// first `Prompt` or `RetryStart` frame, then zero or more `ResumeApproval` / `Cancel`
// control frames, while the server streams typed `Event` envelopes for the
// lifetime of the run, terminating in a `result` event.
//
// The `Event` message mirrors the domain `session.Event` taxonomy
// (engine/session/event.go) one-for-one: a string `type` plus the
// structured submessages (ToolCall, ToolResult, PermissionAsk, Result,
// Usage). It is the single, provider-neutral event schema shared by the
// gRPC and HTTP/SSE adapters; it is never an OpenAI type.
//
// Validation: required-field annotations are authored with
// `buf.validate.field` for documentation and future runtime enforcement.
// V1 enforces the required-field checks in the Go server (see
// internal/adapter/server); wiring the protovalidate runtime is a deferred
// follow-up and is not required for the WP10 milestone.

